        "original_id": "21fe2d34-5067-5c67-85d2-f6347e3a3ebe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Fraser-Smith, Ian Fleming, James Bond, Q\n- Roles: author, missionary, quartermaster\n- Organizations: British Secret Service, Q Branch, Q Division\n- Concepts: fictional characters, film novelisations, research and development\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Fraser-Smith was born on 26 January 1904 and died on 9 November 1992.\n- Charles Fraser-Smith was an author and a one-time missionary.\n- Charles Fraser-Smith is widely credited as the inspiration for Ian Fleming's James Bond quartermaster Q.\n- Q is a fictional character in the James Bond films and film novelisations.\n- Q is the head of Q Branch, later called Q Division, the fictional research and development division of the British Secret Service.",
